# Line-ending policy.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true and had NO .gitattributes, so every
# tracked shell script would be checked out with CRLF. That is not cosmetic: a hook or script whose
# shebang line ends in \r fails with "bad interpreter", and git runs .git/hooks/* directly. The
# pre-commit gate would therefore have silently not run on any fresh clone — the same failure mode
# (a gate that exists but never fires) that made the gate necessary in the first place.
#
# Force LF for everything executed by a POSIX shell or interpreter, regardless of platform.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
hooks/*     text eol=lf

# Batch files are executed by cmd.exe and want CRLF.
*.bat       text eol=crlf

# The observation matrix is line-oriented evidence; keep it diffable and stable across platforms.
*.jsonl     text eol=lf
